{"title":"Encode String With Shortest Length","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"Given a string s, encode the string such that its encoded length is the shortest.\nThe encoding rule is: k[encoded_string], where the encoded_string inside the square brackets is being repeated exactly k times. k should be a positive integer.\nIf an encoding process does not make the string shorter, then do not encode it. If there are several shortest encodings, return the lexicographically smallest one. Only use a repeated-block encoding when it is strictly shorter than the decoded substring. Return s unchanged if no encoding is shorter than s.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: s = \"aaa\"\nOutput: \"aaa\"\n```\n\nThere is no way to encode it such that it is shorter than the input string, so we do not encode it.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: s = \"aaaaa\"\nOutput: \"5[a]\"\n```\n\n\"5[a]\" is shorter than \"aaaaa\" by 1 character.\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: s = \"aaaaaaaaaa\"\nOutput: \"10[a]\"\n```\n\n\"10[a]\" is the lexicographically smallest shortest encoding.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= s.length <= 150\n- s consists of only lowercase English letters.\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def encode(self, s: str) -> str:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().encode","parameters":[{"name":"s","type":"str"}],"returnType":"str","tests":[{"input":["a"],"expected":"a"},{"input":["aa"],"expected":"aa"},{"input":["aaa"],"expected":"aaa"},{"input":["aaaa"],"expected":"aaaa"},{"input":["aaaaa"],"expected":"5[a]"},{"input":["aaaaaa"],"expected":"6[a]"},{"input":["aaaaaaa"],"expected":"7[a]"},{"input":["aaaaaaaaa"],"expected":"9[a]"},{"input":["aaaaaaaaaa"],"expected":"10[a]"},{"input":["aaaaaaaaaaaaaa"],"expected":"14[a]"},{"input":["aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"],"expected":"16[a]"},{"input":["aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"],"expected":"18[a]"},{"input":["aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa